    "description": "Write the baseline of 0.20.0: recall 0.619, precision 0.517 at two repeats\n\n## Summary\n\n- `eval/baseline.json` now measures the defaults of 0.20.0. Posted recall is 0.619 and posted precision is 0.517, at two repeats of the 28 pinned cases (pin `373266b`). The cost is $4.34 for each case, with $0.14 of judge calls. No repeat failed.\n- The margins stay 0.05 and 0.05 by the README rule. The spread is 0.013 for recall and 0.010 for precision.\n- `docs/research/baseline-0-20.md` gives the figures against S1 and the old baseline, and the walle and websites cases apart. It also gives the review time, the posted findings by severity, the false posted findings, the escalation, the sources of the precision cost, and what the stage experiments did not predict.\n- TICKETS.md: D9 names the false posted findings as its target (66.5 in each repeat; 17 of 26 on the walle and websites cases). The R1 line says that the gate baseline now measures 0.20.0.\n\n| | New (0.20.0) | S1 (0.15.0, 1 repeat) | Old baseline (0.10.0) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Posted recall | 0.619 | 0.570 | 0.542 |\n| Posted precision | 0.517 | 0.534 | 0.598 |\n| Cost for each case | $4.34 | $5.56 | $4.66 |\n| Review time, median | 1.1 min | 1.7 min | not recorded |\n\nPrecision is 0.081 under the old baseline file. Most of that gap is older than D4c: S1 gave 0.534 on the old defaults. The user saw these figures and accepts the baseline.\n\nThe PR holds no code, so it has no version change.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `npm test` (1708 passed), `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build`\n- [x] `test/eval-pin.test.ts`: the `cases_ref` of the baseline equals the pin, at two repeats\n- [x] The run: `eval --repeat 2 --write-baseline --resume` on a frozen build of d342898, in five windows, $250.80\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01XrBTZg7V9Qr9viaw1dTW3s\n",
